<title>USA: Sony's &quot;Maguire&quot; wins close U.S. box office race.</title>
<headline>Sony's &quot;Maguire&quot; wins close U.S. box office race.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1997-01-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following are the final</p>
<p>data for the top 10 movies at the U.S. box office during the</p>
<p>weekend Jan. 24-26, according to Exhibitor Relations Co.</p>
<p>    Film		   Three-day gross    Cumulative Gross</p>
<p>1. Jerry Maguire	     $5,518,727	 $109,785,743</p>
<p>2. In Love and War	   $5,489,245	   $5,494,725</p>
<p>3. Beverly Hills Ninja     $5,481,640	  $18,967,251</p>
<p>4. Metro			 $5,479,213	  $18,734,917</p>
<p>5. Evita			 $5,415,891	  $30,465,756</p>
<p>6. Scream			$4,040,199	  $64,593,256</p>
<p>7. The Relic		   $4,008,970	  $25,268,537</p>
<p>8. Fierce Creatures	  $3,759,480	  $  ----</p>
<p>9. Michael		     $3,130,599	  $76,652,206</p>
<p>10 Zeus and Roxanne	  $2,755,382	  $  ----</p>
<p>NOTE: &quot;Jerry Maguire&quot; and &quot;Beverly Hills Ninja&quot; are released by TriStar Pictures, a unit of Sony Corp.</p>
<p>&quot;In Love and War&quot; and &quot;Michael&quot; are released by New Line Cinema, both units of Time Warner Inc..</p>
<p>&quot;Metro&quot; and &quot;Evita&quot; are released by Walt Disney Co.</p>
<p>&quot;Scream&quot; is released by Disney-owned Miramax Films.</p>
<p>&quot;The Relic&quot; is released by Paramount Pictures, a unit of Viacom Inc.</p>
<p>&quot;Fierce Creatures&quot; is released by Universal Pictures, a unit of Seagram Co. Ltd.</p>
<p>&quot;Zeus and Roxanne&quot; is released by MGM, which is owned by financier Kirk Kerkorian and Australia's Seven Network Ltd.</p>
</text>
